OS Version, Kernel Version and Release Information.

Explanation:

Command - Purpose
cat /etc/os-release - Displays operating system information.
uname -r - Displays the kernel release version.
uname -v - Displays kernel build information.
uname -m - Displays system architecture.
uname -s - Displays operating system name.


Important concepts:

/etc/os-release - contains Linux distribution information.
uname - displays system and kernel information.
-r - represents kernel release.
-v - represents kernel version/build information.
-m - represents machine architecture.
-s - represents kernel name.
